=== layout: one-panel

# The Project Transition

@body

- Your individual projects are complete.
- Now use the pitches, feedback, and executive summaries to choose a shared company.
- [*Nov 12:* groups formed.]{color=red}
- *Nov 19:* select your group project by completing the Company Vision Report (Form).
- *Dec 10:* group presentations.
- *Dec 17:* group business plan due.

=== layout: one-panel

# This Week's Work

@body

- Set #5: Medicinal Biotechnology is tonight's topic.
- Complete the movie form assigned this week; check Blackboard for its link and deadline.
- Start conversations about your group and possible company proposals.
- Next week: Set #6, group formation, and Homework 5.

=== layout: one-panel

# Talking Points: One Slide, One Minute

@body

- Research your assigned topic and bring one useful angle to the class.
- Use relevant images, short phrases, and your own words.
- Put detailed speaking notes in the presenter notes.
- If another student shares your topic, add a different example or explanation.
- Ask thoughtful questions and make connections in the chat.

@citation

https://vosslab.github.io/syllabus/fall_2026/biotech/TALKING_POINTS/

=== layout: one-panel

# Discussion Marks

@body

- Be ready to contribute when class starts.
- Ask a clarifying question, explain your reasoning, or connect two ideas.
- Listen to the other presenters; build on what they say.
- A greeting or agreement alone is not a discussion contribution.
- Use your proper first name or a consistent nickname in Zoom.

